ShackLink docs/usrp_b210_support.md 9.30: the AD9361 TX quadrature calibration surveyed on a B210.

UHD_TXQC_LOG=<file>  one line per TX quad cal run: the chip's convergence flags (0x0A7 TX1, 0x0A8 TX2)
                     and the correction words left in 0x08E..0x09D, with why it ran (window | chains).
UHD_TXQC_RESET=1     pulse the cal's soft reset before each run (ADI's order).
UHD_TXQC_SWEEP=1     after each stock run, all 32 RX NCO phase offsets, then the stock 0x15 again.
All unset: UHD's own register writes (one redundant 0x0A0 write). Driven by ShackLinkUsrp.UhdProbe --txqc.

